# pc64onativedisk - opt-in E6 O-only profile without #c and without #S.
#
# This is pc64oconsole (E5: no legacy "cons" registration) with the "sd"
# line also deliberately absent from the dev section.  The generated
# devtab[] therefore registers neither consdevtab nor sddevtab.  Disk
# discovery, unit probing and native O block I/O come directly from the
# SD core (sys/src/9/port/sdcore.c) and the concrete controller drivers
# listed under misc; pc64/main.c calls sdinitcontrollers() after
# chandevreset(), and the core's one-shot guard prevents a second probe.
#
# sdloop is deliberately excluded: its backing store is an inherited
# Chan to a file (namec/devtab read/write).  It remains in the legacy
# configurations.  sdram is kept; it is a concrete SDifc with no Chan.
